findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged unused dependencies but not the inline-version-instead-of-workspace
    issue. The Dev phase added 'chrono and uuid workspace dependencies' but the other
    6 inline deps were not caught.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase mentioned FieldErrorCode or #[non_exhaustive] on any enum in
    the server crate.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote tests checking trace_id exists in meta but no test asserts it
    derives from request context. Dev hardcoded 'none' and it passed.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer LOW finding: 'No structured logging/tracing anywhere \u2014\
    \ all of src/. tracing is listed as a dependency but never used. No #[instrument],\
    \ no tracing::info!(), no span creation.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer did not flag misleading SECURITY comments claiming logging exists
    when it doesn't.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test was written for non-ASCII characters in X-Tenant-ID header. TEA
    security tests cover null bytes and long URIs but not non-ASCII header values.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests but the reviewer noted the test only checks status
    code. However, the reviewer's finding about request_id propagation is a different
    test. The CWE-209 body gap was not explicitly flagged.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS preflight test appears in the TEA output. CORS was not tested
    at all.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No logging was implemented so the wrong-log-level issue doesn't apply
    yet, but no phase established the correct pattern or wrote tests enforcing warn!
    for 4xx vs error! for 5xx.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS middleware was implemented or tested. No phase flagged CWE-942
    or overly permissive CORS configuration.
